{title: Jeds Other Poem}
{artist: Grandaddy}
{key: Em}

{c: Verse 1}
You [Em]Said Id Wake Up Dead Drunk,        Alone In The [F]Park
I Called You A [C]Liar,        But How Right You [G]Were
[Em]Air Conditioned Tv Land, 20 Grand,        Walk To The [F]Bank
With [C]Shakes From The Night Before,        Staring At The [G]Tiki Floor
[Em]High School Wedding Ring,        Keys Are Under The [F]Mats
Of All The [C]Houses Here,        But Not [G]Motels
I [Em]Try To Sing It Funny Like Beck,        But Its Bringing Me [F]Down
Lower Than [C]Ground,        Beautiful [G]Ground
Beautiful [Dm]Ground [Am] [F] [C],        [Dm] [Am] [F] [C]
[Dm] Test Tones And [Am] Failed
Clones And [F]Odd Parts Made [Fm]You
